earnings of $9.25 per share and revenue of $406.05 billion, which would represent changes of +93.92% and +88.04%, respectively, from the prior year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Sales growth 88% (a growth rate, not a level)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027)\",\n     \"whose\": \"Zacks Investment Research (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Zacks Investment Research)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-143\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > this fiscal year (fy2027)\",\n       \"line\": \"sales growth: **88%** | basis: Zacks-stated expectation for NVIDIA; growth rate, not a level | source as stored: Zacks Investment Research | period as stored: this fiscal year (FY2027) | said: not stored | article 136\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 136,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Earnings are expected to rise 93.9% this fiscal year on sales growth of 88%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Sales growth 88% (consensus expectation)\",\n     \"period\": \"this year\",\n     \"whose\": \"Consensus analysts (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Consensus analysts; said 2026-09-29)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-144\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > this year\",\n       \"line\": \"sales growth: **88%** | basis: consensus expectation | source as stored: Consensus analysts | period as stored: this year | said: 2026-09-29 | article 218\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 218,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Analysts continue to raise their earnings forecasts, with next year's estimate up 22% and revisions moving higher almost unanimously across other periods as well. Sales are expected to climb 88% this year and another 65.5% next year, while earnings are projected to rise 94% and 66%, respectively.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue growth 91% (company-wide)\",\n     \"period\": \"This year (fiscal 2027, as framed by the article)\",\n     \"whose\": \"Wall Street consensus (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Wall Street consensus (analysts))\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-145\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > this year (fiscal 2027, as framed by the article)\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth: **91%** | basis: Wall Street consensus expectation; company-wide revenue growth | source as stored: Wall Street consensus (analysts) | period as stored: This year (fiscal 2027, as framed by the article) | said: not stored | article 50\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 50,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Because of its central position in the AI boom, Nvidia is growing much faster than the S&P 500. Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue growth roughly 90% or more\",\n     \"period\": \"current fiscal year\",\n     \"whose\": \"forecaster not named: expectations reported by qz.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: not stored)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-130\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > current fiscal year\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue growth: **roughly 90% or more** | basis: expectations reported by qz.com; forecaster not named | source as stored: not stored | period as stored: current fiscal year | said: not stored | article 16\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 16,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Consensus revenue forecast $111.3 billion (above the top of the company's $108 billion plus or minus 2% guidance range)\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q3 2027\",\n     \"whose\": \"Consensus of analysts, unnamed (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Consensus of analysts (unnamed))\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-124\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"consensus revenue forecast: **$111.3 billion** | basis: consensus forecast, above the top of the company's $108 billion plus or minus 2% guidance range | source as stored: Consensus of analysts (unnamed) | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: not stored | article 232\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 232,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The consensus forecast for that quarter is $111.3 billion, above the top of that range.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Consensus revenue $109.02 billion (+91.2% / +91.24% versus the year-ago quarter)\",\n     \"period\": \"'Current quarter' (T-131, said 2026-09-22); 'upcoming quarter' (T-146)\",\n     \"whose\": \"Zacks Consensus Estimate (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate) / Zacks Consensus (Zacks Investment Research))\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-131\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > current quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Consensus sales estimate: **$109.02 billion** | basis: Consensus revenue, versus year-ago quarter (+91.2%), as reported by Zacks | source as stored: Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate) | period as stored: Current quarter | said: 2026-09-22 | article 11\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 11,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-146\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > upcoming quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$109.02 billion** | basis: Zacks latest consensus estimate; +91.24% versus the year-ago quarter | source as stored: Zacks Consensus (Zacks Investment Research) | period as stored: upcoming quarter | said: not stored | article 231\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 231,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Analysts and investors alike will be keeping a close eye on the performance of Nvidia in its upcoming earnings disclosure. The company's upcoming EPS is projected at $2.47, signifying a 90.00% increase compared to the same quarter of the previous year. Simultaneously, our latest consensus estimate expects the revenue to be $109.02 billion, showing a 91.24% escalation compared to the year-ago quarter.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Consensus revenue estimate $109.0 billion; up 91.2% year over year\",\n     \"period\": \"Next quarter (Q3 fiscal 2027, report expected late November 2026)\",\n     \"whose\": \"Analyst consensus as reported by fool.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Analyst consensus (as reported by fool.com))\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-136\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > next quarter (q3 fiscal 2027, report expected late november 2026)\",\n       \"line\": \"Consensus revenue estimate: **$109.0 billion** | basis: Consensus; up 91.2% from the previous year | source as stored: Analyst consensus (as reported by fool.com) | period as stored: Next quarter (Q3 fiscal 2027, report expected late November 2026) | said: not stored | article 73\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 73,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia is expected to report another strong quarter when it next reports earnings (likely in late November), with the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year. And more of the same is expected for next year, following the Vera Rubin ramp-up.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-135\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > next quarter (q3 fiscal 2027)\",\n       \"line\": \"Year-over-year revenue growth (consensus): **91.2%** | basis: Consensus | source as stored: Analyst consensus (as reported by fool.com) | period as stored: Next quarter (Q3 fiscal 2027) | said: not stored | article 73\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 73,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia is expected to report another strong quarter when it next reports earnings (likely in late November), with the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year. And more of the same is expected for next year, following the Vera Rubin ramp-up.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Q3 revenue growth +91.2% year over year (consensus expected change)\",\n     \"period\": \"Q3 2026\",\n     \"whose\": \"Zacks consensus (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Zacks (consensus analyst estimate))\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-140\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > q3 2026\",\n       \"line\": \"Q3 revenue growth (year over year): **+91.2%** | basis: consensus expected year-over-year change | source as stored: Zacks (consensus analyst estimate) | period as stored: Q3 2026 | said: not stored | article 171\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 171,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's Q3 earnings are expected to increase +90% year-over-year on +91.2% higher revenues, while the year-over-year earnings and revenue growth for Micron is expected to be +938% and +349.5%, respectively.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue growth more than 80% (comparison basis not stated)\",\n     \"period\": \"third quarter (fiscal year not stated)\",\n     \"whose\": \"analysts, unnamed, as reported by finance.yahoo.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: analysts (unnamed), as reported by finance.yahoo.com)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-142\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); the stored source is on each line > third quarter (fiscal year not stated)\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue growth: **more than 80%** | basis: Analysts' expectation as reported by the article; comparison basis (e.g. year-over-year) not stated | source as stored: analysts (unnamed), as reported by finance.yahoo.com | period as stored: third quarter (fiscal year not stated) | said: not stored | article 235\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 235,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The firm sits at the center of an AI infrastructure cycle that analysts expect to push its third-quarter revenue up more than 80%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"b\",\n     \"value\": \"Consensus revenue estimate $92.37 billion (the quarter has since been reported: T-062 stores $96.22 billion)\",\n     \"period\": \"Second quarter\",\n     \"whose\": \"Wall Street consensus per the line's basis; the section stores it as NVIDIA's own estimate (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own estimate (estimate); source as stored: NVIDIA; said about 1 month ago)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-115\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own estimate (estimate) > second quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Consensus revenue estimate: **$92.37 billion** | basis: Wall Street consensus | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Second quarter | said: about 1 month ago | article 201\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 201,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"According to a company press release and earnings commentary, Nvidia reported revenue of $96.22 billion for the second quarter, up 106% year-over-year, alongside adjusted earnings per share of $2.22. Both figures surpassed Wall Street consensus estimates, which called for revenue of $92.37 billion and adjusted earnings of $2.09 per share.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Total revenue $96.2 billion (also stored as $96.22 billion and as $96 billion); up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027 (quarter ended July 26, 2026) in T-007, T-017 to T-022, T-026 to T-028; the same figure is also stored under relative labels: 'Fiscal Q2' (T-030), 'Fiscal second quarter' (T-035), 'latest reported quarter' (T-044, T-047), 'Q2' (T-053), 'Reported quarter (not named in the item)' (T-059), 'second quarter' (T-061, T-062, T-066), 'The quarter' (T-069)\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation / Nvidia)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-007\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Consolidated revenues: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Consolidated; up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 35\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 35,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-017\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$96 billion** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 | said: not stored | article 232\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 232,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Management said fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96 billion more than doubled from a year earlier. Growth also sped up for the fourth quarter in a row.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-018\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$96.2 billion** | stored from 7 articles, each with its own details: || article 37: basis: record; quarter ended July 26, 2026 | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 53: basis: company total | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 (quarter ended July 26, 2026) | said: not stored || article 73: basis: Company total; up 106% from a year ago | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 (quarter ended 26 July 2026) | said: not stored || article 78: basis: Company total; up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 121: basis: Company total revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26, 2026) | said: not stored || article 139: basis: up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially; company-reported | source as stored: NVIDIA Corp. | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 151: basis: as reported | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 (quarter ended July 2026) | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\",\n          \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 53,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26) was another exceptional one. Revenue grew 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, an acceleration from the previous quarter, and the data center business contributed all but about $7 billion of the total. Profit kept up. Net income rose 126% year over year, to $59.7 billion.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 73,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"What stands out in Nvidia's most recent earnings report is that the company is still growing at a triple-digit rate. Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (ending July 26, 2026) was $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago. Of that, $89 billion, or roughly 92.5% of the company's total revenue, came from its data center segment.\",\n          \"Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126% from a year ago, and earnings per share of $2.46 were up 128% from last year. Nvidia is very profitable -- its operating expenses totaled only $8.4 billion for the quarter, and its gross margin was an impressive 75%.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 78,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\",\n          \"Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 121,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 139,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release. Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 151,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-019\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$96.22 billion** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 46: basis: up 105.85% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored || article 54: basis: Company total; up 105.8% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 46,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 54,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%.\",\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-020\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth: **106%** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 37: basis: year-over-year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 151: basis: increase as reported, year-over-year comparison implied by the article | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\",\n          \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 151,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-021\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth: **18%** | basis: sequential | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 37\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\",\n          \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-022\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth year over year: **106%** | basis: Company total, versus a year earlier | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26, 2026) | said: not stored | article 121\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 121,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-026\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"revenues: **$96.22 billion** | basis: up 106% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: second quarter of fiscal 2027 | said: not stored | article 92\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 92,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-027\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"total revenue: **$96 billion** | basis: company total | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 | said: not stored | article 115\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 115,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA’s data center revenue was $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, out of $96 billion in total.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-028\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Total revenues: **$96 billion** | basis: Total company, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 122\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 122,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA’s Data Center segment remained its key growth driver, with revenues surging 117% year over year to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the company’s Aug. 26 press release. Total revenues reached an exceptional $96 billion, representing a 106% year-over-year and 18% sequential jump.\",\n          \"Along with revenue growth, the company’s profitability has also strengthened. NVIDIA’s gross margin rose to 75% from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased. NVIDIA’s GAAP operating income has more than doubled year over year, implying significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-030\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > fiscal q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Company-level revenue, as reported by the article | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: Fiscal Q2 | said: not stored | article 162\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 162,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"In its fiscal Q2, Nvidia's revenue grew at a 106% year-over-year pace to $96.2 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-035\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$96.2 billion** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 22: basis: Company total, more than doubled year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal second quarter | said: not stored || article 55: basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal second quarter | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 22,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue surging 117% to $89 billion,\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 55,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year.\",\n          \"The company also produced a 75% gross margin\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-044\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Total revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Company-wide revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: latest reported quarter | said: not stored | article 13\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 13,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"That is an eye-catching demonstration, but the scale gap remains enormous: Nvidia's latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion overall, meaning roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-047\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter (unspecified)\",\n       \"line\": \"Total revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Company total | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Latest reported quarter (unspecified) | said: not stored | article 39\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 39,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest quarter puts the scale of the contest in perspective: data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in revenue, or roughly 92.5%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-053\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Company revenue as stated; article compares year-over-year growth with SpaceX | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 | said: not stored | article 80\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 80,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia posted an even stronger quarter; revenue was up 106% year over year to $96.2 billion. It converted $63.7 billion of that into operating income, showcasing its impressive profitability.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-059\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > reported quarter (not named in the item)\",\n       \"line\": \"quarterly revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: NVIDIA Corporation, quarterly | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: Reported quarter (not named in the item) | said: not stored | article 74\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 74,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-061\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > second quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: Nvidia total company revenue as reported | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: second quarter | said: not stored | article 143\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 143,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"During the second quarter, Nvidia generated $96.2 billion in revenue.\",\n          \"More than 90% of Nvidia's revenue comes from its data center division, so Nvidia's quarterly revenue figures nearly exceed what Broadcom expects to generate from AI semiconductors during FY 2027.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-062\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > second quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$96.22 billion** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Second quarter | said: about 1 month ago | article 201\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 201,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"According to a company press release and earnings commentary, Nvidia reported revenue of $96.22 billion for the second quarter, up 106% year-over-year, alongside adjusted earnings per share of $2.22. Both figures surpassed Wall Street consensus estimates, which called for revenue of $92.37 billion and adjusted earnings of $2.09 per share.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-066\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > second quarter (q2)\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$96.2 billion** | basis: company-wide quarterly revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: second quarter (Q2) | said: not stored | article 147\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 147,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"During the second quarter, Nvidia generated $96.2 billion in revenue.\",\n          null\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-069\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > the quarter (period not further specified in the item)\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$96.2B** | basis: Company total, as stated in the item | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: The quarter (period not further specified in the item) | said: not stored | article 95\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 95,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA (NVDA) posted $96.2B revenue; data center sales were $89B, about 92.5% of total — key revenue driver for the quarter.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Data Center segment revenue $89 billion (also stored as $89.02 billion and $89.023 billion); up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially; roughly 92.5% of total revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal Q2 2027 (quarter ended July 26, 2026) in T-008 to T-013; the same figure is also stored under relative labels: 'Fiscal second quarter' (T-033), 'latest reported quarter' (T-041 to T-043, T-045, T-046), 'Reported quarter (not named in the item)' (T-056), 'The quarter' (T-067, T-068)\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation / Nvidia)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-008\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenue: **$89 billion** | stored from 5 articles, each with its own details: || article 37: basis: segment; up 117% year-over-year; majority of total revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 78: basis: Data Center segment; up 117% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 115: basis: data center segment | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 | said: not stored || article 121: basis: Data center segment, share of total revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26, 2026) | said: not stored || article 139: basis: up 117% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA Corp. | period as stored: fiscal Q2 2027 | said: 2026-08-26\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\",\n          \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 78,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\",\n          \"Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 115,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA’s data center revenue was $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, out of $96 billion in total.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 121,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 139,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release. Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-009\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenue: **$89.023 billion** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored | article 46\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 46,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-010\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenue growth: **117%** | basis: year-over-year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 37\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\",\n          \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-011\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenues: **$89.02 billion** | basis: up 117% year over year; segment | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: second quarter of fiscal 2027 | said: not stored | article 92\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 92,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-012\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data center segment revenue: **$89 billion** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 73: basis: Segment; roughly 92.5% of total revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q2 fiscal 2027 (quarter ended 26 July 2026) | said: not stored || article 122: basis: Data Center segment, up 117% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 73,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"What stands out in Nvidia's most recent earnings report is that the company is still growing at a triple-digit rate. Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (ending July 26, 2026) was $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago. Of that, $89 billion, or roughly 92.5% of the company's total revenue, came from its data center segment.\",\n          \"Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126% from a year ago, and earnings per share of $2.46 were up 128% from last year. Nvidia is very profitable -- its operating expenses totaled only $8.4 billion for the quarter, and its gross margin was an impressive 75%.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 122,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA’s Data Center segment remained its key growth driver, with revenues surging 117% year over year to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the company’s Aug. 26 press release. Total revenues reached an exceptional $96 billion, representing a 106% year-over-year and 18% sequential jump.\",\n          \"Along with revenue growth, the company’s profitability has also strengthened. NVIDIA’s gross margin rose to 75% from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased. NVIDIA’s GAAP operating income has more than doubled year over year, implying significant operating leverage.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-013\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q2\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center segment revenues: **$89 billion** | basis: Data Center segment; up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal second quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 35\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 35,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\",\n          \"NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-033\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Data center revenue: **$89 billion** | basis: Data center segment, up 117% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal second quarter | said: not stored | article 22\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 22,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue surging 117% to $89 billion,\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-041\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"data center revenue: **$89 billion** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 114: basis: quarterly data center segment revenue, up 117% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: latest reported quarter | said: not stored || article 116: basis: data center segment, latest quarter | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: latest reported quarter | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 114,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"According to the latest prints, Nvidia's quarterly data center revenue is now $89 billion -- up 117% year over year.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 116,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Revenue in its latest quarter also more than doubled, with almost all of it coming from data center customers, and management's outlook for the current quarter assumes no data center compute sales to China at all.\",\n          \"Nvidia's data center business brought in $89 billion in its latest quarter alone, and management guided the next quarter to $108 billion, excluding any China compute sales.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-042\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Data-center revenue: **$89 billion** | basis: Data-center segment revenue, as reported in the company's quarterly results | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: latest reported quarter | said: not stored | article 13\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 13,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"That is an eye-catching demonstration, but the scale gap remains enormous: Nvidia's latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion overall, meaning roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-043\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Data-center share of total sales: **roughly 92.5%** | basis: Data-center revenue divided by total revenue, as calculated by GuruFocus | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: latest reported quarter | said: not stored | article 13\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 13,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"That is an eye-catching demonstration, but the scale gap remains enormous: Nvidia's latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion overall, meaning roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-045\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter (unspecified)\",\n       \"line\": \"Data center revenue: **$89 billion** | basis: Data center segment revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Latest reported quarter (unspecified) | said: not stored | article 39\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 39,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest quarter puts the scale of the contest in perspective: data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in revenue, or roughly 92.5%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-046\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > latest reported quarter (unspecified)\",\n       \"line\": \"Data center share of revenue: **roughly 92.5%** | basis: Data center revenue as a share of total revenue (approximately) | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Latest reported quarter (unspecified) | said: not stored | article 39\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 39,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest quarter puts the scale of the contest in perspective: data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in revenue, or roughly 92.5%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-056\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > reported quarter (not named in the item)\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenue: **$89.0 billion** | basis: rising 117% | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: Reported quarter (not named in the item) | said: not stored | article 74\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 74,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-067\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > the quarter (period not further specified in the item)\",\n       \"line\": \"data center sales: **$89B** | basis: Data center segment | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: The quarter (period not further specified in the item) | said: not stored | article 95\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 95,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA (NVDA) posted $96.2B revenue; data center sales were $89B, about 92.5% of total — key revenue driver for the quarter.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-068\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > the quarter (period not further specified in the item)\",\n       \"line\": \"data center share of total revenue: **about 92.5% of total** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: The quarter (period not further specified in the item) | said: not stored | article 95\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 95,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA (NVDA) posted $96.2B revenue; data center sales were $89B, about 92.5% of total — key revenue driver for the quarter.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue $178 billion (company-wide; up 96% year over year)\",\n     \"period\": \"First half of fiscal 2027 (ended July 26, 2026)\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: Nvidia)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-029\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > first half of fiscal 2027 (ended july 26, 2026)\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$178 billion** | basis: Company-wide revenue, up 96% year over year | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: First half of fiscal 2027 (ended July 26, 2026) | said: not stored | article 105\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 105,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"For now, Nvidia remains primarily focused on AI. In the first half of its fiscal 2027 (which ended July 26), its revenue rose by 96% year over year to $178 billion. Also, due to the relatively slower growth in its costs and expenses, its net income surged by 161% to $118 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue growth 85% year over year (company total; no revenue amount is stored for this quarter)\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first quarter (T-005, T-006); stored as 'previous quarter (Q1 FY2027)' in T-052\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / Nvidia)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-005\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q1\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue growth: **85%** | basis: year over year, company total | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal 2027 first quarter | said: not stored | article 96\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 96,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year, while Data Center revenues jumped 92%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-006\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q1\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth year over year: **85%** | basis: Prior quarter, versus a year earlier | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal 2027 first quarter | said: not stored | article 121\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 121,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-052\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > previous quarter (q1 fy2027)\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue growth: **85% rate** | basis: year-over-year rate | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: previous quarter (Q1 FY2027) | said: not stored | article 141\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 141,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Over the three months ended July 26 (its fiscal 2027 second quarter), it earned $59.7 billion, more than twice its year-ago profit. And revenue growth accelerated to 106% year over year, up from the previous quarter's 85% rate.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Data Center revenues growth 92% year over year (Data Center segment; no revenue amount is stored for this quarter)\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2027 first quarter\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-004\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2027-Q1\",\n       \"line\": \"Data Center revenues growth: **92%** | basis: year over year, Data Center segment | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal 2027 first quarter | said: not stored | article 96\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 96,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year, while Data Center revenues jumped 92%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"c\",\n     \"value\": \"Revenue $215.9 billion (T-037 stores 'close to $215.9 billion'); up roughly 65.5% year over year; company total\",\n     \"period\": \"fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026) in T-001; stored as 'Fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026' in T-037, T-038\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / Nvidia)\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-001\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > FY2026\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **$215.9 billion** | basis: company total; up roughly 65.5% year over year | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal 2026 (ended January 2026) | said: not stored | article 116\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 116,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"In fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, revenue reached nearly $215.9 billion, up roughly 65.5% year over year. This scale produced net income of approximately $120.1 billion. The net margin remained remarkably high at approximately 55.6%, consistent with the 55.8% net margin achieved in the previous fiscal year.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-037\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > fiscal year ended jan. 25, 2026\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue: **close to $215.9 billion** | basis: Company, fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026 | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: Fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026 | said: not stored | article 229\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 229,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"In the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, revenue reached close to $215.9 billion, a massive increase of approximately 65.5% year over year. Net income for the period was nearly $120.1 billion, producing a net margin of roughly 55.6%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-038\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual) > fiscal year ended jan. 25, 2026\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue growth, year over year: **approximately 65.5%** | basis: Company, fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026 | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: Fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026 | said: not stored | article 229\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 229,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"In the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, revenue reached close to $215.9 billion, a massive increase of approximately 65.5% year over year. Net income for the period was nearly $120.1 billion, producing a net margin of roughly 55.6%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ],\n   \"S3\": [\n    {\n     \"group\": \"a\",\n     \"value\": \"$108 billion, plus or minus 2%; total revenue guidance\",\n     \"period\": \"Fiscal third quarter of 2027 / Q3 fiscal 2027 / fiscal Q3 2027 / third quarter of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA; NVIDIA Corporation; NVIDIA Corp.; Nvidia\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-083\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"Projected revenues: **$108 billion, plus or minus 2%** | basis: Company guidance; midpoint implies a 12% sequential rise | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal third quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 35\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 35,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA further expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027. At the midpoint, this would represent a 12% sequential rise.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-084\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$108 billion** | basis: plus or minus 2% | source as stored: NVIDIA Corp. | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 | article 139\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 139,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.\",\n          \"In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-085\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue guidance: **$108 billion** | stored from 7 articles, each with its own details: || article 37: basis: plus or minus 2%; assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q3 fiscal 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 46: basis: excludes China Data Center compute revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q3 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored || article 54: basis: Midpoint of guidance | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Q3 fiscal 2027 | said: not stored || article 115: basis: company total, plus or minus 2% | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: not stored || article 121: basis: Company outlook; about 12% above fiscal second-quarter revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal 2027 third quarter | said: not stored || article 122: basis: Plus or minus 2% | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal third quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 177: basis: plus or minus 2%; company-wide; results due 17 November 2026 | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 37,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Furthermore, Nvidia issued an even stronger outlook. For Q3 fiscal 2027, the company expects revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. Importantly, the forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. Nvidia expects GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 46,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Management guided Q3 to $108 billion.\",\n          \"Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue citing geopolitical uncertainty.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 54,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%.\",\n          \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 115,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Management guided fiscal Q3 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. That midpoint is about 12% above the Q2 total.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 121,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The forecasts go far past the quarter. Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 122,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Looking ahead, NVIDIA projects $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in revenues for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, signaling continued sequential growth. Profitability is also expected to remain robust, and with the Vera Rubin platform entering full production, NVIDIA is well-poised to benefit from the next phase of demand for AI infrastructure.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 177,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA reports its fiscal Q3 2027 results after the market closes on November 17, 2026. Management has guided revenue to $108 billion , plus or minus 2%.\",\n          \"On November 17, watch whether revenue clears the low end of that guide, about $106 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-086\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue guidance: **$108 billion, plus or minus 2%** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 78: basis: Company total, company outlook | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: fiscal third quarter of 2027 | said: 2026-08-26 || article 232: basis: company guidance | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 78,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.\",\n          \"In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 232,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Management guided revenue for that quarter to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-087\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue guidance: **$108.0 billion** | basis: company revenue guidance | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: fiscal Q3 2027 | said: not stored | article 53\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 53,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"And management guided for another step up in this quarter (fiscal Q3): $108.0 billion of revenue.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-088\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > FY2027-Q3\",\n       \"line\": \"revenues guidance: **$108 billion (+/- 2%)** | basis: indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: third quarter of fiscal 2027 | said: not stored | article 92\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 92,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"The company expects third-quarter revenues of $108 billion (+/- 2%), indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"a\",\n     \"value\": \"around 70% revenue growth\",\n     \"period\": \"FY 2027\",\n     \"whose\": \"Nvidia; NVIDIA\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-104\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > fy 2027\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue growth: **around 70%** | stored from 2 articles, each with its own details: || article 143: basis: Nvidia estimate as cited for the full fiscal year | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: FY 2027 | said: not stored || article 147: basis: company revenue growth estimate, as stated | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: FY 2027 | said: not stored\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 143,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"For FY 2027, Nvidia estimates its revenue growth will be around 70%.\"\n         ]\n        },\n        {\n         \"article\": 147,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"For FY 2027, Nvidia estimates its revenue growth will be around 70%. While this is slower than Broadcom's AI semiconductor growth rate, it's still very fast.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"group\": \"a\",\n     \"value\": \"$108 billion revenue\",\n     \"period\": \"current quarter / Current quarter / Fiscal third quarter / next quarter / Q3 / Third quarter / third quarter (Q3)\",\n     \"whose\": \"NVIDIA; Nvidia; NVIDIA Corporation\",\n     \"note\": null,\n     \"cited_lines\": [\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-100\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > current quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue: **$108 billion** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: current quarter | said: not stored | article 55\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 55,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-101\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > current quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue forecast for the current quarter: **$108 billion** | basis: Company forecast; assumes no China data-center chip revenue | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Current quarter | said: not stored | article 163\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 163,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Nvidia's $108 billion forecast for the current quarter assumes no China data-center chip revenue, the company says. Any sales there would come on top of that outlook.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-103\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > fiscal third quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue guidance: **approximately $108 billion** | basis: Company guidance; implied 89% growth is the article's calculation | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: Fiscal third quarter | said: not stored | article 22\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 22,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"management has guided for approximately $108 billion in third-quarter revenue, implying 89% growth\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-107\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > next quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"Revenue guidance: **$108 billion** | basis: company outlook excluding any China data center compute sales | source as stored: NVIDIA | period as stored: next quarter | said: not stored | article 116\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 116,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Revenue in its latest quarter also more than doubled, with almost all of it coming from data center customers, and management's outlook for the current quarter assumes no data center compute sales to China at all.\",\n          \"Nvidia's data center business brought in $89 billion in its latest quarter alone, and management guided the next quarter to $108 billion, excluding any China compute sales.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-110\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > q3\",\n       \"line\": \"revenue guidance: **$108 billion** | basis: Nvidia company-wide revenue outlook as cited | source as stored: Nvidia | period as stored: Q3 | said: not stored | article 143\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 143,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"For Q3, it expects $108 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-111\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance) > third quarter\",\n       \"line\": \"third-quarter revenue outlook: **$108 billion** | basis: not stored | source as stored: NVIDIA Corporation | period as stored: Third quarter | said: not stored | article 74\",\n       \"stored_passages\": [\n        {\n         \"article\": 74,\n         \"passages\": [\n          \"Its third-quarter revenue outlook is $108 billion.\"\n         ]\n        }\n       ]\n      },\n      {\n       \"id\": \"T-112\",\n       \"under\": \"Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook 