. 25, 2026, revenue reached close to $215.9 billion, a massive increase of approximately 65.5% year over year. Net income for the period was nearly $120.1 billion, producing a net margin of roughly 55.6%.'])]), ('T-038', [(229, ['In the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, revenue reached close to $215.9 billion, a massive increase of approximately 65.5% year over year. Net income for the period was nearly $120.1 billion, producing a net margin of roughly 55.6%.'])])]\n\n S2\nANSWER Revenue guidance $108 billion, plus or minus 2% (company total; assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China; the bases give the midpoint as about 12% above fiscal Q2 and about 89.5% up year over year) | fiscal Q3 2027 (stored as Q3 fiscal 2027 / fiscal third quarter of 2027) in T-083 to T-088; the same $108 billion is also stored under relative labels: 'current quarter' (T-100, T-101), 'next quarter' (T-107), 'Fiscal third quarter' (T-103), 'Q3' (T-110), 'Third quarter' (T-111), 'third quarter (Q3)' (T-112) | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation / Nvidia; said 2026-08-26 where stored) | None \n [('T-083', [(35, ['NVIDIA further expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027. At the midpoint, this would represent a 12% sequential rise.'])]), ('T-084', [(139, ['NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.', 'In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.'])]), ('T-085', [(37, ['Furthermore, Nvidia issued an even stronger outlook. For Q3 fiscal 2027, the company expects revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. Importantly, the forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. Nvidia expects GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.']), (46, ['Management guided Q3 to $108 billion.', 'Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue citing geopolitical uncertainty.']), (54, ['Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%.', \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"]), (115, ['Management guided fiscal Q3 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. That midpoint is about 12% above the Q2 total.']), (121, ['The forecasts go far past the quarter. Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.']), (122, ['Looking ahead, NVIDIA projects $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in revenues for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, signaling continued sequential growth. Profitability is also expected to remain robust, and with the Vera Rubin platform entering full production, NVIDIA is well-poised to benefit from the next phase of demand for AI infrastructure.']), (177, ['NVIDIA reports its fiscal Q3 2027 results after the market closes on November 17, 2026. Management has guided revenue to $108 billion , plus or minus 2%.', 'On November 17, watch whether revenue clears the low end of that guide, about $106 billion.'])]), ('T-086', [(78, ['NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.', 'In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.']), (232, ['Management guided revenue for that quarter to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.'])]), ('T-087', [(53, ['And management guided for another step up in this quarter (fiscal Q3): $108.0 billion of revenue.'])]), ('T-088', [(92, ['The company expects third-quarter revenues of $108 billion (+/- 2%), indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.'])]), ('T-100', [(55, ['Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.'])]), ('T-101', [(163, [\"Nvidia's $108 billion forecast for the current quarter assumes no China data-center chip revenue, the company says. Any sales there would come on top of that outlook.\"])]), ('T-103', [(22, ['management has guided for approximately $108 billion in third-quarter revenue, implying 89% growth'])]), ('T-107', [(116, [\"Revenue in its latest quarter also more than doubled, with almost all of it coming from data center customers, and management's outlook for the current quarter assumes no data center compute sales to China at all.\", \"Nvidia's data center business brought in $89 billion in its latest quarter alone, and management guided the next quarter to $108 billion, excluding any China compute sales.\"])]), ('T-110', [(143, ['For Q3, it expects $108 billion.'])]), ('T-111', [(74, ['Its third-quarter revenue outlook is $108 billion.'])]), ('T-112', [(147, ['For Q3, it expects $108 billion.'])])]\nANSWER Revenue growth 17%, sequential (for the same guide, T-083, T-085 and T-088 store about 12% sequential) | current quarter | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA) | None \n [('T-102', [(55, ['Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.'])])]\nANSWER Prior revenue guidance $91 billion, plus or minus 2% | Q2 fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA; said 2026-08-26) | None \n [('T-076', [(37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"])])]\nANSWER Revenue growth around 70% (basis: Nvidia estimate as cited for the full fiscal year) | FY 2027 (as stored; T-093 to T-099 store the same about-70% company growth figure for fiscal 2028) | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: Nvidia / NVIDIA) | None \n [('T-104', [(143, ['For FY 2027, Nvidia estimates its revenue growth will be around 70%.']), (147, [\"For FY 2027, Nvidia estimates its revenue growth will be around 70%. While this is slower than Broadcom's AI semiconductor growth rate, it's still very fast.\"])])]\nANSWER Vera Rubin share of data center revenue about 20% (management expectation; a share, not a revenue amount) | fiscal Q3 2027 | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA) | None \n [('T-089', [(177, ['Management expects Vera Rubin to bring in about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.']), (232, ['The newly launched Vera Rubin platform is one source of that revenue. Management expects it to make up about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.'])])]\nANSWER Revenue around $412 billion | Fiscal 2027 | Analysts' c