t year, while earnings are projected to rise 94% and 66%, respectively.\"])])]\nANSWER Revenue growth 91% (company-wide) | This year (fiscal 2027, as framed by the article) | Wall Street consensus (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Wall Street consensus (analysts)) | None \n [('T-145', [(50, ['Because of its central position in the AI boom, Nvidia is growing much faster than the S&P 500. Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.'])])]\nANSWER Revenue growth roughly 90% or more | current fiscal year | forecaster not named: expectations reported by qz.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: not stored) | None \n [('T-130', [(16, [\"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"])])]\nANSWER Consensus revenue forecast $111.3 billion (above the top of the company's $108 billion plus or minus 2% guidance range) | fiscal Q3 2027 | Consensus of analysts, unnamed (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Consensus of analysts (unnamed)) | None \n [('T-124', [(232, ['The consensus forecast for that quarter is $111.3 billion, above the top of that range.'])])]\nANSWER Consensus revenue $109.02 billion (+91.2% / +91.24% versus the year-ago quarter) | 'Current quarter' (T-131, said 2026-09-22); 'upcoming quarter' (T-146) | Zacks Consensus Estimate (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Zacks Investment Research (Zacks Consensus Estimate) / Zacks Consensus (Zacks Investment Research)) | None \n [('T-131', [(11, ['For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%.'])]), ('T-146', [(231, [\"Analysts and investors alike will be keeping a close eye on the performance of Nvidia in its upcoming earnings disclosure. The company's upcoming EPS is projected at $2.47, signifying a 90.00% increase compared to the same quarter of the previous year. Simultaneously, our latest consensus estimate expects the revenue to be $109.02 billion, showing a 91.24% escalation compared to the year-ago quarter.\"])])]\nANSWER Consensus revenue estimate $109.0 billion; up 91.2% year over year | Next quarter (Q3 fiscal 2027, report expected late November 2026) | Analyst consensus as reported by fool.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Analyst consensus (as reported by fool.com)) | None \n [('T-136', [(73, ['Nvidia is expected to report another strong quarter when it next reports earnings (likely in late November), with the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year. And more of the same is expected for next year, following the Vera Rubin ramp-up.'])]), ('T-135', [(73, ['Nvidia is expected to report another strong quarter when it next reports earnings (likely in late November), with the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year. And more of the same is expected for next year, following the Vera Rubin ramp-up.'])])]\nANSWER Q3 revenue growth +91.2% year over year (consensus expected change) | Q3 2026 | Zacks consensus (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Zacks (consensus analyst estimate)) | None \n [('T-140', [(171, [\"Nvidia's Q3 earnings are expected to increase +90% year-over-year on +91.2% higher revenues, while the year-over-year earnings and revenue growth for Micron is expected to be +938% and +349.5%, respectively.\"])])]\nANSWER Revenue growth more than 80% (comparison basis not stated) | third quarter (fiscal year not stated) | analysts, unnamed, as reported by finance.yahoo.com (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: analysts (unnamed), as reported by finance.yahoo.com) | None \n [('T-142', [(235, ['The firm sits at the center of an AI infrastructure cycle that analysts expect to push its third-quarter revenue up more than 80%.'])])]\nANSWER Consensus revenue estimate $92.37 billion (the quarter has since been reported: T-062 stores $96.22 billion) | Second quarter | Wall Street consensus per the line's basis; the section stores it as NVIDIA's own estimate (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own estimate (estimate); source as stored: NVIDIA; said about 1 month ago) | None \n [('T-115', [(201, ['According to a company press release and earnings commentary, Nvidia reported revenue of $96.22 billion for the second quarter, up 106% year-over-year, alongside adjusted earnings per share of $2.22. Both figures surpassed Wall Street consensus estimates, which called for revenue of $92.37 billion and adjusted earnings of $2.09 per share.'])])]\nANSWER Total revenue $96.2 billion (also stored as $96.22 billion and as $96 billion); up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially | fiscal Q2 2027 (quarter ended July 26, 2026) in T-007, T-017 to T-022, T-026 to T-028; the same figure is also stored under relative labels: 'Fiscal Q2' (T-030), 'Fiscal second quarter' (T-035), 'latest reported quarter' (T-044, T-047), 'Q2' (T-053), 'Reported quarter (not named in the item)' (T-059), 'second quarter' (T-061, T-062, T-066), 'The quarter' (T-069) | NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation / Nvidia) | None \n [('T-007', [(35, [\"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\", \"NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"])]), ('T-017', [(232, ['Management said fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96 billion more than doubled from a year earlier. Growth also sped up for the fourth quarter in a row.'])]), ('T-018', [(37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"]), (53, [\"Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26) was another exceptional one. Revenue grew 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, an acceleration from the previous quarter, and the data center business contributed all but about $7 billion of the total. Profit kept up. Net income rose 126% year over year, to $59.7 billion.\"]), (73, [\"What stands out in Nvidia's most recent earnings report is that the company is still growing at a triple-digit rate. Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (ending July 26, 2026) was $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago. Of that, $89 billion, or roughly 92.5% of the company's total revenue, came from its data center segment.\", 'Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126% from a year ago, and earnings per share of $2.46 were up 128% from last year. Nvidia is very profitable -- its operating expenses totaled only $8.4 billion for the quarter, and its gross margin was an impressive 75%.']), (78, [\"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\", 'Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.', \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"]), (121, [\"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"]), (139, [\"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release. Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\", \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"]), (151, ['Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.'])]), ('T-019', [(46, ['Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.']), (54, ['Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%.', \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"])]), ('T-020', [(37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"]), (151, ['Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.'])]), ('T-021', [(37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"])]), ('T-022', [(121, [\"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"])]), ('T-026', [(92, ['NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.'])]), ('T-027', [(115, ['NVIDIA’s data center revenue was $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, out of $96 billion in total.'])]), ('T-028', [(122, ['NVIDIA’s Data Center segment remained its key growth driver, with revenues surging 117% year over year to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the company’s Aug. 26 press release. Total revenues reached an exceptional $96 billion, representing a 106% year-over-year and 18% sequential jump.', 'Along with revenue growth, the company’s profitability has also strengthened. NVIDIA’s gross margin rose to 75% from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased. NVIDIA’s GAAP operating income has more than doubled year over year, implying significant operating leverage.'])]), ('T-030', [(162, [\"In its fiscal Q2, Nvidia's revenue grew at a 106% year-over-year pace to $96.2 billion.\"])]), ('T-035', [(22, ['Fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue surging 117% to $89 billion,']), (55, ['Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year.', 'The company also produced a 75% gross margin'])]), ('T-044', [(13, [\"That is an eye-catching demonstration, but the scale gap remains enormous: Nvidia's latest quarter generated $89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion overall, meaning roughly 92.5% of sales came from the infrastructure businesses powering large-scale AI.\"])]), ('T-047', [(39, [\"Nvidia's latest quarter puts the scale of the contest in perspective: data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in revenue, or roughly 92.5%.\"])]), ('T-053', [(80, ['Nvidia posted an even stronger quarter; revenue was up 106% year over year to $96.2 billion. It converted $63.7 billion of that into operating income, showcasing its impressive profitability.'])]), ('T-059', [(74, ['NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.'])]), ('T-061', [(143, ['During the second quarter, Nvidia generated $96.2 billion in revenue.', \"More than 90% of Nvidia's revenue comes from its data center division, so Nvidia's quarterly revenue figures nearly excee