t P/E multiple of about 24x appear rather attractive.']), (92, ['NVIDIA also expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, although supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.']), (98, ['For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead. That guide does not depend on finding more demand. The CEO says demand is much greater than 70%, and that supply is what holds the guide there.']), (177, ['Management’s preliminary outlook is for revenue to grow about 70% in fiscal 2028. Management called that outlook supply-constrained. Demand without that limit would be a lot higher, management said.'])]), ('T-095', [(121, ['And on the company\\'s late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \"a supply-constrained outlook.\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.']), (222, ['The lower multiple comes despite Nvidia forecasting roughly 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028 as demand for AI training and inference continues to drive its business.'])]), ('T-096', [(54, ['Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%.', \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"])]), ('T-097', [(22, ['while CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — a figure that far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled'])]), ('T-098', [(53, [\"On the company's earnings call in late August, chief financial officer Colette Kress went a whole year further.\", '\"We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028,\" Kress said. \"This is a supply-constrained outlook.\"'])]), ('T-099', [(45, ['In its fiscal 2027 second-quarter report, Management forecast that in fiscal 2028, its sales will rise by 70%, thanks to continued demand for AI chips.', \"But what's really interesting is that Nvidia leadership said it could double its sales in fiscal 2028 if it were able to overcome the constraints on the supply of commodities needed to produce its hardware.\", \"On Nvidia's second-quarter fiscal 2027 earnings call , Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said:\", 'Incredibly, we are seeing demand acceleration even at our scale. Customer forecasts point to our growth doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply-constrained.'])]), ('T-105', [(55, ['management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year'])]), ('T-106', [(166, ['This is for a company with about 75% gross margins that grew its revenue by more than 100% last quarter and projected that it would increase its revenue by around 70% next fiscal year.'])]), ('T-108', [(162, ['Nvidia projects this supply/demand situation will continue, contributing to a 70% revenue growth forecast for next year.'])]), ('T-109', [(158, [\"Next year, its management team believes the company will grow revenue at a 70% pace. If you've followed Nvidia throughout the AI race, you know that management often sandbags its guidance, so the real growth rate is likely higher than this.\"])])]\nANSWER Year-on-year revenue growth 70% (Nvidia forecast as described by Morningstar) | not stored | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: Nvidia) | None \n [('T-113', [(32, ['Lost in a torrent of news about Nvidia NVDA this year—its role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments , its forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth , and its acquisition of Hugging Face —was a dividend announcement.'])])]\nANSWER Chip sales to double (NVIDIA chip sales) | next year | Jensen Huang; the basis calls it a forecast attributed to CEO Jensen 