(177, ['In August 2026, management said rising memory costs will cut NVIDIA’s gross margin, the share of sales kept after production costs.', 'Management expects gross margin to hit its low in fiscal Q4 2027, at 71% to 72%. It was 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Memory is the cause: management said memory prices rose more than it had expected.']), (232, ['For fiscal Q3 2027 it is guided to 74%, plus or minus half a point, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Management pointed to higher component costs, especially memory.'])]), ('T-034', [(55, ['Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year.', 'The company also produced a 75% gross margin'])]), ('T-039', [(16, [\"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"])]), ('T-058', [(74, ['NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.'])]), ('T-075', [(166, ['This is for a company with about 75% gross margins that grew its revenue by more than 100% last quarter and projected that it would increase its revenue by around 70% next fiscal year.'])])]\nANSWER Non-GAAP gross margin 75% (versus 72.5% in the prior-year quarter) | Q2 fiscal 2027 ('Fiscal second quarter of 2027' in article 35) | NVIDIA, reported (actual section; source as stored NVIDIA; said 2026-08-26) | None \n [('T-016', [(35, [\"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\", \"NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"]), (37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"])])]\nANSWER Gross margin change: 2.5 percentage points of expansion (GAAP/non-GAAP basis not specified) | Q2 fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA, reported (actual section; source as stored NVIDIA) | None \n [('T-015', [(151, ['Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.'])])]\n\n S4\nANSWER Gross margin 72% to 73% (company gross margin guidance, lowered on higher-than-expected memory costs; helped by price increases taking effect in fiscal Q1 2028) | Fiscal 2028 | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA management / NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress) / NVIDIA; said late August 2026 where stored) | None \n [('T-092', [(98, ['Gross margin is guided lower. Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.']), (121, [\"Margins might not change the picture much, either. On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"]), (177, ['NVIDIA has already set price increases that take effect in fiscal Q1 2028. Management expects those higher prices to lift margin to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028.'])])]\nANSWER Gross margin 71% to 72% (expected low point / trough, caused by higher memory prices) | fiscal Q4 2027 (stored as fiscal Q4 2027 / Fiscal 2027 fourth quarter) | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress); said August 2026 / late August 2026 where stored) | None \n [('T-090', [(115, ['Memory prices rose more than NVIDIA expected, and NVIDIA reset its margin expectations. Gross margin is the share of sales left after production costs. NVIDIA guided it to 74% for fiscal Q3, down from 75% in Q2. NVIDIA expects gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4.']), (177, ['In August 2026, management said rising memory costs will cut NVIDIA’s gross margin, the share of sales kept after production costs.', 'Management expects gross margin to hit its low in fiscal Q4 2027, at 71% to 72%. It was 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Memory is the cause: management said memory prices rose more than it had expected.'])]), ('T-091', [(121, [\"Margins might not change the picture much, either. On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"])])]\nANSWER Gross margin approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points (GAAP and non-GAAP; low end 73.5%; down from fiscal Q2 2027, management cited higher component costs, especially memory) | fiscal Q3 2027 (stored as Q3 fiscal 2027 / fiscal Q3 2027 / fiscal third quarter of 2027) | NVIDIA's own outlook (section: Stored as NVIDIA's own outlook (guidance); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation; said 2026-08-26 where stored) | None \n [('T-077', [(37, ['Furthermore, Nvidia issued an even stronger outlook. For Q3 fiscal 2027, the company expects revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. Importantly, the forecast assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China. Nvidia expects GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of approximately 74%, plus or minus 50 basis points.'])]), ('T-078', [(115, ['Memory prices rose more than NVIDIA expected, and NVIDIA reset its margin expectations. Gross margin is the share of sales left after production costs. NVIDIA guided it to 74% for fiscal Q3, down from 75% in Q2. NVIDIA expects gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4.'])]), ('T-079', [(232, ['For fiscal Q3 2027 it is guided to 74%, plus or minus half a point, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Management pointed to higher component costs, especially memory.'])]), ('T-080', [(177, ['On November 17, watch fiscal Q3 2027 gross margin against 73.5%, the low end of management’s gross margin guide for that quarter.'])]), ('T-081', [(139, ['NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.', 'In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.'])]), ('T-082', [(78, ['NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth.', 'In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.'])])]\nANSWER Gross margin 72% to 73% (as volumes scale; the same range the table stores as NVIDIA's own outlook in T-092) | fiscal 2028 | 24/7 Wall St. (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: 24/7 Wall St.) | None \n [('T-125', [(46, ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'])])]\nANSWER Gross margin 71% to 72% (expected to bottom on memory cost inflation; the same range the table stores as NVIDIA's own outlook for fiscal Q4 2027 in T-090, T-091) | Q4 | 24/7 Wall St. (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: 24/7 Wall St.) | None \n [('T-141', [(46, ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'])])]\nANSWER Gross margin under 72% (recovery expected thereafter) | fourth quarter | analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg (section: Stored as someone else's forecast (estimate); source as stored: Bloomberg (analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg)) | None \n [('T-132', [(16, [\"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"])])]\nANSWER Gross margin 75% (one article's basis says GAAP; up from 72.4% a year ago; T-015 stores an expansion of 2.5 percentage points, GAAP/non-GAAP basis not specified) | fiscal Q2 2027 (quarter ended 26 July 2026) in T-014, T-015; the same 75% is also stored under 'fiscal second quarter' (T-034), 'last quarter' (T-039), 'Reported quarter (not named in the item)' (T-058) and with no period as 'about 75%' (T-075) | NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corporation / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress)) | None \n [('T-014', [(73, [\"What stands out in Nvidia's most recent earnings report is that the company is still growing at a triple-digit rate. Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (ending July 26, 2026) was $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago. Of that, $89 billion, or roughly 92.5% of the company's total revenue, came from its data center segment.\", 'Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126% from a year ago, and earnings per share of $2.46 were up 128% from last year. Nvidia is very profitable -- its operating expenses totaled only $8.4 billion for the quarter, and its gross margin was an impressive 75%.']), (78, [\"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\", 'Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.', \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"]), (115, ['Memory prices rose more than NVIDIA expected, and NVIDIA reset its margin expectations. Gross margin is the share of sales left after production costs. NVIDIA guided it to 74% for fiscal Q3, down from 75% in Q2. NVIDIA expects gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4.']), (121, [\"Margins might not change the picture much, either. On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"]), (122, ['NVIDIA’s Data Center segment remained its key growth driver, with revenues surging 117% year over year to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the company’s Aug. 26 press release. Total revenues reached an exceptional $96 billion, representing a 106% year-over-year and 18% sequential jump.', 'Along with revenue growth, the company’s profitability has also strengthened. NVIDIA’s gross margin rose to 75% from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased. NVIDIA’s GAAP operating income has more than doubled year over year, implying significant operating leverage.']), (139, [\"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release. Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand.\", \"NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"]), (177, ['In August 2026, management said rising memory costs will cut NVIDIA’s gross margin, the share of sales kept after production costs.', 'Management expects gross margin to hit its low in fiscal Q4 2027, at 71% to 72%. It was 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Memory is the cause: management said memory prices rose more than it had expected.']), (232, ['For fiscal Q3 2027 it is guided to 74%, plus or minus half a point, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Management pointed to higher component costs, especially memory.'])]), ('T-015', [(151, ['Nvidia reported exceptional financial results in the second quarter of fiscal 2027, which ended in July 2026. Revenue increased 106% to $96.2 billion, gross margin expanded 2.5 percentage points, and non-GAAP net income rose 120% to $2.22 per diluted share.'])]), ('T-034', [(55, ['Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year.', 'The company also produced a 75% gross margin'])]), ('T-039', [(16, [\"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"])]), ('T-058', [(74, ['NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.'])]), ('T-075', [(166, ['This is for a company with about 75% gross margins that grew its revenue by more than 100% last quarter and projected that it would increase its revenue by around 70% next fiscal year.'])])]\nANSWER Non-GAAP gross margin 75% (versus 72.5% in the prior-year quarter) | fiscal Q2 2027 (stored as Fiscal second quarter of 2027 / Q2 fiscal 2027) | NVIDIA, reported (section: Stored as reported by NVIDIA (actual); source as stored: NVIDIA; said 2026-08-26) | None \n [('T-016', [(35, [\"The Data Center segment remains NVIDIA's primary growth engine, with revenues jumping 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, according to the Aug. 26 press release. Consolidated revenues soared to $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\", \"NVIDIA's non-GAAP gross margin increased to 75% in the fiscal second quarter compared with 72.5% a year ago.\"]), (37, [\"Nvidia delivered another blockbuster quarter, reporting its fiscal second-quarter 2027 results on Aug. 26, for the quarter ended July 26. Revenue reached a record $96.2 billion, up 106% year-over-year (YoY) from $46.7 billion, and increased 18% sequentially. The result also comfortably exceeded Nvidia's prior guidance of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\", \"The company's profitability expanded even faster. On a non-GAAP basis, net income climbed 118% to $54 billion, versus $24.8 billion in Q2 fiscal 2026, while adjusted EPS jumped 120% to $2.22, exceeding expectations. Non-GAAP gross margin rose to 75% from 72.5%. Operating income surged 124% YoY to $63.7 billion.\", \"Nvidia's Data Center segment remained the primary growth engine, generating $89 billion in revenue, up 117% YoY from the prior-year quarter and representing the majority of total company revenue. The performance reflects continued demand for Nvidia's accelerated-computing platforms as hyperscalers and AI companies expand infrastructure.\"])])]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record-3/week-compare-packet-settle.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",m[\\\"matter\\\"]),[print(\\\"KEY\\\",k[\\\"id\\\"],k[\\\"value\\\"],\\\"|\\\",k[\\\"period\\\"],\\\"|\\\",k[\\\"whose\\\"],k[\\\"articles\\\"]) for k in m[\\\"key\\\"]],[(print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",s),[print(a[\\\"value\\\"],\\\"|\\\",a[\\\"period\\\"],\\\"|\\\",a[\\\"whose\\\"],\\\"|\\\", \\\",\\\".join(l[\\\"id\\\"]+\\\":\\\"+\\\"/\\\".join(str(x[\\\"article\\\"]) for x in l[\\\"stored_passages\\\"]) for l in a[\\\"cited_lines\\\"])) for a in ans if a[\\\"group\\\"] in (\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\")]) for s,ans in m[\\\"sets\\\"].items()]) for m in p]' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/record-3/week-compare-packet-settle.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",m[\\\"matter\\\"]),[print(\\\"KEY\\\",k[\\\"id\\\"],k[\\\"value\\\"],\\\"|\\\",k[\\\"period\\\"],\\\"|\\\",k[\\\"whose\\\"],k[\\\"articles\\\"]) for k in m[\\\"key\\\"]],[(print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",s),[print(a[\\\"value\\\"],\\\"|\\\",a[\\\"period\\\"],\\\"|\\\",a[\\\"whose\\\"],\\\"|\\\", \\\",\\\".join(l[\\\"id\\\"]+\\\":\\\"+\\\"/\\\".join(str(x[\\\"article\\\"]) for x in l[\\\"stored_passages\\\"]) for l in a[\\\"cited_lines\\\"])) for a in ans if a[\\\"group\\\"] in (\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\")]) for s,ans in m[\\\"sets\\\"].items()]) for m in p]' \"","aggregated_output":"\n M01\nKEY M01-K1 $108 billion, plus or minus 2% | the fiscal third quarter of 2027 | the company (its guide) [35, 92, 121]\nKEY M01-K2 $406.05 billion (an 88% year-over-year rise) | fiscal 2027 | the Zacks Consensus Estimate [92]\nKEY M01-K3 around $412 billion | fiscal 2027 | analysts' consensus [121]\nKEY M01-K4 revenue growth of roughly 90% (or more) | the current fiscal year (the article writes no fiscal year number) | an expectation the article does not attribute [16, 121]\nKEY M01-K5 $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year | the quarter of the next earnings report (the article writes no fiscal quarter) | consensus [73]\n\n S1\nRevenue guidance $108 billion, plus or minus 2% (company total; assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China; midpoint implies about a 12% sequential rise and 89.5% year-over-year growth) | Q3 fiscal 2027 (also stored as 'Fiscal third quarter of 2027', 'third quarter of fiscal 2027', 'fiscal Q3 2027') | NVIDIA, its own outlook (guidance section; source as stored NVIDIA / NVIDIA Corp. / NVIDIA Corporation; said 2026-08-26) | T-083:35,T-084:139,T-085:37/46/54/115/121/122/177,T-086:78/232,T-087:53,T-08