ss) | period as stored: Fiscal 2028 | said: not stored | article 22 [(22, ['while CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — a figure that far exceeded the 45% Wall Street had previously modeled'])]\nT-137 revenue growth: **70%** | basis: Company-wide revenue growth expectation cited by the author, unattributed to a named analyst or to company guidance | source as stored: Keithen Drury (fool.com) | period as stored: next year | said: 2026-09-26 | article 140 [(140, [\"This could eat into Nvidia's business over the next few years, but with Nvidia expected to grow its revenue at a 70% pace during next year, I'd say it's doing just fine.\"])]\nT-125 gross margin: **72% to 73%** | basis: as volumes scale | source as stored: 24/7 Wall St. | period as stored: fiscal 2028 | said: not stored | article 46 [(46, ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'])]\nT-141 gross margin: **71% to 72%** | basis: expected to bottom on memory cost inflation | source as stored: 24/7 Wall St. | period as stored: Q4 | said: not stored | article 46 [(46, ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'])]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
